  "execution_contract": {
    "objective": "Q1 pooled conformal groupwise diagnostic plus Q2 pre-registered policy-weight sensitivity; no formal claim or model replacement.",
    "q1_design": "Use the existing training/validation/blind split and fixed HGBR point predictions. Compare pooled normalized split-conformal with region-by-task-type calibration; report pooled and 18-group coverage, absolute deviation from 0.95, interval width, and unchanged WAPE/RMSE.",
    "q1_acceptance": "Only propose groupwise adoption if worst-group absolute coverage deviation improves by at least 0.02, pooled coverage remains within [0.90,0.99], and mean interval width inflation is at most 25%; otherwise explicitly retain pooled intervals.",
    "q2_design": "Run the same full-horizon Q2 candidate and FIFO control for the pre-registered policy grid: current (1,4,0.015,0.015,0.05), cost-lean (2,2,0.015,0.015,0.05), carbon-lean (0.5,8,0.015,0.015,0.05), and latency-guarded (1,4,0.03,0.03,0.05). Reuse only the declared supplied inputs and keep all hard constraints identical.",
    "q2_acceptance": "Every variant must have task completion 1, SLA violation 0, and all hard audits passed. A policy is a candidate for main-model review only if it is non-dominated on cost/carbon/latency versus current and improves a primary target by at least 0.25% without worsening another primary metric by more than 0.25%; otherwise retain the current policy and report the Pareto trade-off.",
    "reproducibility": "Record commands, environment, seed, input/code hashes, runtime, metric units, baseline, and all negative or rejected findings. Do not call any policy globally optimal or causal."
  }
